@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — A Popkin's level decides what is sent
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
participant "DispatchNotificationsJob" as job
box "Backend — Popkin Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "DispatchNotificationsCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "NotificationRules" as rules
end box
box "Backend — Popkin Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Popkin database" as db
end box
job -> handler : Send DispatchNotificationsCommand (every 15 s)
handler -> db : New NotificationEvent rows; each recipient's Membership.NotificationLevel
db --> handler : Event (Kind, PopkinId, RecipientPersonId?) and levels
handler -> rules : LevelAllows(level, kind, isForThePerson)
note right of rules
  Everything: every kind.
  JustForMe: MentionsAndReplies, DirectMessages,
  PlanChanges that give the person a story,
  and the Reminders kinds (L2-158 AC2).
  Muted: StoriesDue and PopkinWrappingUp only (L2-158 AC3).
  A wrapped-up Popkin: nothing but its recap (L2-158 AC5).
end note
rules --> handler : Allowed, or Suppressed(PopkinMuted or JustForMe)
handler -> db : NotificationDelivery Pending or Suppressed
@enduml
